WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.944
Once upon a time, there was a kindhearted girl.

2
00:00:05.944 --> 00:00:14.266
Her evil stepmother would not let her go to the prince's ball.

3
00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:20.190
But a fairy godmother came to the rescue.

4
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.071
Can you guess what story this is?

5
00:00:24.071 --> 00:00:29.318
Here's a hint: there is a glass shoe.

6
00:00:29.319 --> 00:00:34.158
That's right! The story is "Cinderella."

7
00:00:34.158 --> 00:00:37.909
"Cinderella" is a very old fairy tale.

8
00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:41.988
In fact, it's over a thousand years old.

9
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:48.457
But the glass shoe and the fairy godmother only appeared around three hundred years ago.

10
00:00:48.457 --> 00:00:54.028
This version of "Cinderella" was published in France in 1697.

11
00:00:54.029 --> 00:00:58.762
It introduced most of the details that are familiar today.

12
00:00:58.763 --> 00:01:01.858
A pumpkin becomes a carriage.

13
00:01:01.858 --> 00:01:05.808
Mice are turned into horses.

14
00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:21.135
And the fairy godmother's magic wears off at midnight.

15
00:01:21.135 --> 00:01:26.236
But this version is very different from earlier "Cinderella" stories.

16
00:01:26.236 --> 00:01:37.358
One of the earliest known "Cinderella" stories appeared in China around 860.

17
00:01:37.358 --> 00:01:43.499
In this story Cinderella wants to go to a festival and not a ball.

18
00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:49.049
And instead of a fairy godmother, there is a magic fish.

19
00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:54.881
Cinderella wears a gown made of sea green silk.

20
00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:58.028
Her cloak is made of feathers.

21
00:01:58.028 --> 00:02:03.997
And her lost shoe is made of gold.

22
00:02:03.998 --> 00:02:10.313
Much later a story called "Kongjwi and Patjwi" was written.

23
00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:13.942
This one comes from Korea.

24
00:02:13.942 --> 00:02:21.013
Kongjwi has an evil stepmother and a stepsister named Patjwi.

25
00:02:21.013 --> 00:02:29.203
The stepmother gives Kongjwi lots of chores so she cannot go to a feast.

26
00:02:29.203 --> 00:02:37.937
A bull, a toad, sparrows, and a fairy all help Kongjwi finish the chores.

27
00:02:37.937 --> 00:02:46.602
On Kongjwi's way to the feast, she loses her silk shoe in a stream.

28
00:02:46.602 --> 00:02:52.333
The local governor finds the lost shoe.

29
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:58.624
He searches for its owner and finds Kongjwi at the feast.

30
00:02:58.624 --> 00:03:06.750
In 1634 the first European version of the story was published in Italy.

31
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:12.233
A fairy lives in a date tree over the grave of Cinderella's mother.

32
00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:18.927
The fairy helps Cinderella attend a ball.

33
00:03:18.927 --> 00:03:24.681
When she loses her shoe, the king finds it.

34
00:03:24.681 --> 00:03:30.643
To find the shoe's owner, he invites the women of the kingdom to a feast.

35
00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:35.072
At the feast the shoe jumps out of the king's hands.

36
00:03:35.073 --> 00:03:41.136
It flies onto Cinderella's foot!

37
00:03:41.136 --> 00:03:45.603
Today even more versions of "Cinderella" exist.

38
00:03:45.603 --> 00:03:48.476
Each story has different details.

39
00:03:48.477 --> 00:03:54.138
But the storyline usually follows the same pattern with a missing shoe.

40
00:03:54.138 --> 00:03:57.863
Can you guess how the story almost always ends?

41
00:03:57.863 --> 00:04:06.109
Yes—Cinderella and her husband live "happily ever after!"

